# Prior-work de-duplication

The repository was searched before promotion.

## Already established elsewhere

- finite-order ambiguity exists in other FIN composition/population-generator
  lanes, including models agreeing through a finite order and differing at the
  next order;
- hidden-state elimination and memory kernels already occur in prior programs;
- detector confusion/loss and calibration premises appear in earlier
  operational-assessment work;
- heat/unitary/wave are already known to be operationally inequivalent despite
  sharing `A`;
- the general equivalence theory of stochastic/probabilistic automata is
  classical (Paz/Carlyle/Tzeng lineage).

## Scoped new contribution of this package

- an explicit **single visible embedded-jump path** alias built directly on the
  strict FIN destination law, with exact horizon formula
  `TV_(L+1)=8 delta^2` and a frozen period-two three-step witness;
- exact lag-one/lag-two identification formulas for a persistent hidden-bit
  alias of the strict embedded-jump chain;
- application of the finite-state equivalence bound to the FIN clock-free path
  protocol, with replayed witness lengths;
- destination-specific `12x12` confusion plus destination-dependent censoring
  inversion for unlabeled cycle recovery, including a linear ordinal confidence
  certificate;
- the **first-nonscalar-jet** carrier criterion plus the spectral-projector
  `P_1=f(A)` counterexample showing that analytic functional calculus alone does
  not preserve carrier adjacency.

No historical result is relabeled as a new fundamental FIN theorem.
